, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed49"}, {"id": "b60be0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4a"}, {"id": "00fa56", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An alternating emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>440</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></math> is applied&nbsp;to a circuit containing an inductance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>. If an a.c. ammeter is connected in the circuit, its reading will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "453457", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4d"}, {"id": "27235a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4e"}, {"id": "9f34cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed4f"}, {"id": "28ac2b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed51", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4712"], "question": {"text": "<p>The current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math> respectively for the given circuit is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F96d424cf-d5b4-40fb-87f6-17984f076b7c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 181px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "346e93", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>55</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed52"}, {"id": "ff7876", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>33</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed53"}, {"id": "09ebe6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>33</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed54"}, {"id": "509b51", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>55</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed56", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "What happens to the inductive reactance and the current in a purely inductive circuit if the frequency is halved ?"}, "options": [{"id": "2ca5f7", "text": "Both, inductive reactance and current will<br />be halved.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed57"}, {"id": "4b768a", "text": "Inductive reactance will be halved and<br />current will be doubled..", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed58"}, {"id": "e27de4", "text": "Inductive reactance will be doubled and<br />current will be halved.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed59"}, {"id": "bf01d8", "text": "Both, inducting reactance and current will be doubled", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the given figures, choose the correct options:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F29a62bfb-4c63-4350-9ed5-313a18649019-9895167q.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 523px; height: 190px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "78f197", "text": "The rms current in circuit (b) can never be larger than that in (a)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5c"}, {"id": "1d8ae0", "text": "The rms current in figure (a) is always equal to that in figure (b)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5d"}, {"id": "17dd3d", "text": "The rms current in circuit (b) can be larger than that in (a)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5e"}, {"id": "695663", "text": "At resonance, current in (b) is less than that in (a)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed5f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed60", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "The RMS&nbsp;value of conduction current in a parallel plate capacitor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The capacity of this capacitor, if it is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>230</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;AC&nbsp;supply with an angular frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, will be"}, "options": [{"id": "8c0571", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>pF</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed61"}, {"id": "ea43dd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mi>pF</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed62"}, {"id": "86ca12", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>pF</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed63"}, {"id": "7b348f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mi>pF</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed64"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed65", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "An LCR circuit is at resonance for a capacitor $C$, inductance $L$ and resistance $R$. Now the value of resistance is halved keeping all other parameters same. The current amplitude at resonance will be now:"}, "options": [{"id": "f1170e", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed66"}, {"id": "5d1c8d", "text": "same", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed67"}, {"id": "b03c79", "text": "halved", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed68"}, {"id": "3ff226", "text": "double", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed69"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance is connected across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>&nbsp;AC supply. The time taken by the current to change from its maximum value to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rms</mi></math> value is:"}, "options": [{"id": "1b874b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6b"}, {"id": "3d0e53", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6c"}, {"id": "1834a9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6d"}, {"id": "eed313", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed6f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4712"], "question": {"text": "<p>A coil of inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is connected to a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. Determine approximately :</p><p>(a) The time elapsed before the current acquires half of its steady-state&nbsp;value<br />(b) The energy stored in the magnetic field associated with the coil at an instant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></math> after the circuit is switched on. (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9ac61d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed70"}, {"id": "0e8fcd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed71"}, {"id": "fa6d59", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed72"}, {"id": "9bcac6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed73"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed74", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An alternating current is given by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>. The rms current will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "3019b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed75"}, {"id": "bf7bd9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed76"}, {"id": "88113d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed77"}, {"id": "fd997e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed78"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed79", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "Match List I with List II\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fcn-rOZnWwajJf1aqI7egAYWztYV-WX07l4dRjn8g6I8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />$\\text { Choose the correct answer from the options given below: }$"}, "options": [{"id": "a172cb", "text": "A-I. B-IV, C-II, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7a"}, {"id": "d905c2", "text": "A-IV. B-I. C-II. D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7b"}, {"id": "0d8a82", "text": "A-IV. B-I, C-III, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7c"}, {"id": "66ebd1", "text": "A-I. B-IV, C-III, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "In series LCR circuit, the capacitance is changed from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>C</mi></math>. To keep the resonance frequency unchanged, the new inductance should be :"}, "options": [{"id": "3d5134", "text": "reduced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>L</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88eed7f"}, {"id": "30e48c", "text": "increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org